            r1_brief: `July 2026. You are the technical manager of the Quilcamayo water-user junta: one river intake, the main canal and 2,440 users. 40 export growers irrigate 3,000 ha of avocado and grape (10,000 m³ per ha; about S/ 40,000 of sales per ha with full water) and 2,400 smallholders 6,000 ha of maize, cotton and vegetables (8,000 m³ per ha; about S/ 9,000 per ha). The town takes 4 hm³ for drinking water and the wetland at the river mouth must receive an ecological flow of 6 hm³; the unlined canal loses 30% of what it receives. The authority expects about 120 hm³ at the intake this season and a 40% chance of a dry year next season. This season water is shared pro rata. Decide the tariff, the canal lining and the drought protocol.`,
